Claude 0.08 (1 Nov 2026)
=========================

A desktop client for Claude, using the Anthropic Messages API.

Requirements
  RISC OS 5 (desktop font text painting needs Wimp 3.80 or later).
  curl with TLS, installed from PackMan and reachable on Run$Path.
  An Anthropic API key from https://console.anthropic.com.
  A claude.ai subscription does not work here: the API bills
  per token, separately.

Use
  Click SELECT on the icon bar icon to open the conversation.
  Type in the field at the top and press Return or click Send.
  MENU over the window: Save conversation, Save reply,
  Save code, Clear, Choices.
  MENU over the icon bar icon: Info, Choices, Quit.

Choices
  Saved to <Choices$Write>.Claude.Choices in plain text,
  API key included.

Updates
  When Claude starts it checks GitHub for a newer release. If
  there is one, a window offers to open the Releases page in your
  browser. Tick "Don't show this message for this update again" to
  skip that release; you still hear about later ones. Untick
  "Check for updates when Claude starts" in Choices to turn the
  check off. The check needs curl and an internet connection, and
  says nothing if either is missing.

Attaching files
  Drag files onto the conversation window or the icon bar icon,
  or click Attach... and drag them into the Attachments window or
  type a pathname. They are sent with your next message.
  Text files are included in full. JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and PDF
  files are sent as images and documents; later messages only
  carry a note that they were attached. Up to 8 files, 3MB in all.
  Convert Sprites and other images to JPEG or PNG first.
  The hourglass shows while files load, and a grey note in the
  conversation confirms each file attached.

Saving
  MENU over the window: Save conversation, Save reply and Save
  code each open a Save as box. Drag its icon to a Filer window,
  or type a full pathname and click Save. Save code saves the
  code blocks from Claude's last reply; BBC BASIC code is saved
  as BASIC text, ready to run.

CLAUDE.md
  Instructions sent to Claude with every message, for example
  "Reply in plain British English". Click Edit... in Choices to
  open it in your text editor; the first time, !Claude creates it
  with starter instructions. Save it in the editor and the change
  applies to your next message. Delete the file to send none.
  Stored as <Choices$Write>.Claude.CLAUDE/md.

Limits
  Text only. No streaming, no attachments, no saved transcripts.
  The conversation lives in memory and is lost on Quit.
  Markdown shows as typed (**bold**, # headings).
  Characters outside Latin-1 show as "?".
